  "plan": "## Implementation Plan: Add Code Path to Board\n\n### Overview\nAdd a `code_path` field to each board's configuration so AI agents know where the associated project code lives. Agents should also have access to a `CONTEXT.md` file for project-level context. When agents are invoked, they should be started with their working directory set to the project root, and their instructions should include the code path and context file path.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Config Schema Changes\n\n#### Global Config (~/.mad/config.json)\nAdd a `code_path` field to store the default project root path:\n```json\n{\n  \"code_path\": \"/home/user/myproject\"\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** The feature description mentions per-board config at `~/.mad/boards/<boardname>/config.json`, but this does not currently exist in the codebase. To keep this implementation focused, we will use a single global `code_path` field. If per-board overrides are needed in the future, they can be added by storing board-specific paths in the global config (e.g., `{\"code_paths\": {\"myboard\": \"/path/to/project\"}}`).\n\n#### Derivation Logic (when code_path is not set)\nIf `code_path` is not configured, derive it from board location using this algorithm:\n1. Get the board path: `<mad_dir>/boards/<boardname>`\n2. Go up two levels: `board_path.parent.parent` = project root\n3. Example: `~/.mad/boards/mad` → project root is `~`\n\n#### Symlink Handling\nResolve symlinks to real paths using `os.path.realpath()` before storing or using `code_path`. This ensures consistent path handling and prevents symlink-based path traversal issues.\n\n---\n\n### 2. CONTEXT.md Location and Handling\n\n**Location Decision:** `<project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n- This places CONTEXT.md alongside the board directory, making it naturally associated with the project\n- This is consistent with the existing `.mad/boards/mad/ideas/CONTEXT.md` structure\n\n**Resolution Order:**\n1. If `code_path` is set, look for `<code_path>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n2. If derived, look at `<derived_path>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n3. If not found, provide empty context (no error)\n\n**Size Handling:**\n- Maximum file size: 100KB\n- If file exceeds limit, truncate with message: `[CONTEXT TRUNCATED - file exceeded 100KB limit]`\n- This prevents loading massive files into agent context\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- If CONTEXT.md cannot be read (permission denied, missing), log a warning and continue with empty context\n- Do not fail the agent invocation if context file is unavailable\n\n---\n\n### 3. Agent Invocation Changes\n\n**Working Directory:**\n- When invoking an agent, set `cwd` to `code_path` (resolved real path)\n- This replaces the current behavior of using the work item directory\n\n**Instruction Prepending:**\n- **Scope:** Prepend context to the INITIAL message/instructions only (when starting a new agent session), NOT on every turn\n- This means when writing the `.tmp/<item>.instructions` file, include the context header at the top\n- The context is written once per agent invocation, not streamed with each message\n\n**Format:**\n```\nCode Path: /home/user/myproject\nContext File: /home/user/myproject/.mad/CONTEXT.md\n\n[existing instructions]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Implementation Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Update Config Schema (pipeline/config.py)\n- Add `code_path` property to Config class\n- Add `get_code_path(board_name)` method that:\n  - Returns configured `code_path` if set\n  - Derives from board location if not set: `boards_dir.parent.parent`\n  - Resolves symlinks with `os.path.realpath()`\n\n#### Step 2: Add Path Validation (new utility function)\n- Create `validate_code_path(path)` function that:\n  - Checks path exists and is accessible\n  - Prevents path escaping (e.g., path cannot resolve to a parent of the expected root)\n  - Block sensitive paths like `/etc`, `~/.ssh`\n- Return error message if validation fails, None if valid\n\n#### Step 3: Create Context Loading Utility (new module: pipeline/context.py)\n- `load_context(code_path)` function that:\n  - Builds path: `<code_path>/.mad/CONTEXT.md`\n  - Reads file if exists\n  - Returns empty string if not found\n  - Handles truncation if >100KB\n  - Returns (content, path) tuple\n\n#### Step 4: Modify Agent Runner (pipeline/runner.py)\n- Update `AgentRunner.__init__` to accept `code_path` parameter\n- Modify `headless()` method to:\n  - Accept optional `code_path` parameter\n  - Load context using context.py utility\n  - Prepend context header to prompt\n  - Use `code_path` as `cwd` instead of workdir\n- Modify `interactive()` method similarly\n\n#### Step 5: Update Pipeline Phases (pipeline/phases.py)\n- When creating AgentRunner, pass the resolved `code_path`\n- Ensure all agent invocations use the project root as working directory\n\n#### Step 6: CLI Commands (optional enhancement)\n- `mad config set-code-path <path>` - Set the code_path in config\n- `mad context edit` - Open CONTEXT.md in editor\n- `mad context show` - Display current CONTEXT.md content\n\n---\n\n### 5. Security Considerations\n\n- **Path Validation:** Validate that `code_path` doesn't escape to parent directories or access sensitive paths\n- **Working Directory:** Setting cwd to project root is safe because:\n  - The agent only operates within the project's codebase\n  - Malicious code would be limited to the project directory\n  - This is the intended behavior (agents should work on the project)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Backward Compatibility\n\n- If `code_path` is not configured, derive from board location (existing behavior)\n- If CONTEXT.md doesn't exist, provide empty context (no disruption)\n- All existing functionality continues to work\n\n---\n\n### 7. Files to Modify\n\n| File | Changes |\n|------|---------|\n| `pipeline/config.py` | Add `code_path` property and `get_code_path()` method |\n| `pipeline/context.py` | NEW: Context loading utility |\n| `pipeline/runner.py` | Accept `code_path`, load context, set working directory |\n| `pipeline/phases.py` | Pass `code_path` to AgentRunner |\n\n---\n\n### 8. Testing\n\n- Test code_path derivation from board location\n- Test symlink resolution\n- Test CONTEXT.md loading, truncation, and missing file handling\n- Test path validation (escape prevention)\n- Test agent working directory is set correctly"
